/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.1 Historical Evolution and Generations of Computing) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A computer is a programmable electronic device that accepts raw data, processes it) Tj
T*
(according to stored instructions, and produces meaningful information:) Tj
T*
(* 1st Generation \(1940-1956\): Vacuum Tubes. Magnetic drums for memory; programmed in) Tj
T*
(raw Machine Language; massive heat dissipation \(e.g., ENIAC, UNIVAC\).) Tj
T*
(* 2nd Generation \(1956-1963\): Transistors. Invented at Bell Labs; smaller, faster,) Tj
T*
(energy-efficient; magnetic core memory; introduction of Assembly & early high-level) Tj
T*
(languages \(FORTRAN, COBOL\).) Tj
T*
(* 3rd Generation \(1964-1971\): Integrated Circuits \(ICs\). Semiconductor chips packing) Tj
T*
(dozens of transistors; keyboards and monitors replaced punched cards; Operating) Tj
T*
(Systems emerged \(IBM System/360\).) Tj
T*
(* 4th Generation \(1971-Present\): Very Large Scale Integration \(VLSI\) & Ultra Large) Tj
T*
(Scale Integration \(ULSI\). Complete CPU integrated onto a single microchip \(Intel 4004) Tj
T*
(in 1971\); personal computers \(PC\), laptops, smartphones.) Tj
T*
(* 5th Generation \(Present and Beyond\): Artificial Intelligence, quantum computing,) Tj
T*
(parallel processing, and neuromorphic computing architectures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.2 Functional Hardware Subsystems of a Digital Computer) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Every digital computer is composed of five interconnected functional units:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Input Unit: Transduces human-readable or physical real-world data into binary) Tj
T*
(electrical signals \(Keyboards, mouse, optical scanners, sensors, ADCs\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Central Processing Unit \(CPU\) - The Brain:) Tj
T*
(- Arithmetic Logic Unit \(ALU\): Executes arithmetic operations \(addition, subtraction,) Tj
T*
(multiplication\) and logical operations \(AND, OR, NOT, comparisons\).) Tj
T*
(- Control Unit \(CU\): The supervisor of the CPU. Fetches instructions sequentially from) Tj
T*
(memory, decodes opcodes, and emits precision micro-electrical timing and control) Tj
T*
(signals.) Tj
T*
(- Register Array: Ultra-high-speed internal CPU storage locations operating at processor) Tj
T*
(clock speed.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Memory Subsystem:) Tj
T*
