/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.3 Computer Architecture Models: Von Neumann vs Harvard) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Von Neumann Architecture \(1945\):) Tj
T*
(- Core Paradigm: Stored-Program Concept. Both machine instructions \(code\) and program) Tj
T*
(data share a single unified memory space and unified system bus.) Tj
T*
(- The Von Neumann Bottleneck: Because code and data share the same physical bus, the CPU) Tj
T*
(cannot fetch an instruction and read/write operand data simultaneously. Throughput is) Tj
T*
(strictly bounded by memory bus throughput.) Tj
T*
(* Harvard Architecture:) Tj
T*
(- Core Paradigm: Physically separated memory banks and dedicated independent buses for) Tj
T*
(instructions and data.) Tj
T*
(- Advantage: Simultaneous instruction fetching and operand memory access, yielding) Tj
T*
(higher execution throughput. Widely implemented in Digital Signal Processors \(DSPs\) and) Tj
T*
(modern CPU L1 caches \(split L1-Instruction and L1-Data caches\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.4 Internal CPU Registers and Machine Instruction Cycle) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Dedicated CPU Registers:) Tj
T*
(- Program Counter \(PC\): Holds the memory address of the next instruction to be fetched.) Tj
T*
(- Memory Address Register \(MAR\): Holds the physical memory address currently being read) Tj
T*
(from or written to.) Tj
T*
(- Memory Data Register \(MDR\) / Memory Buffer Register \(MBR\): Holds the actual) Tj
T*
(data/instruction read from or written to memory.) Tj
T*
(- Instruction Register \(IR\): Holds the fetched instruction word while it is being) Tj
T*
(decoded by the Control Unit.) Tj
T*
(- Accumulator \(ACC\) & General Purpose Registers \(R0-R15\): Hold intermediate mathematical) Tj
T*
(operands and computation results.) Tj
T*
(* The 4-Phase Instruction Execution Cycle:) Tj
T*
(- Phase 1: Fetch \(PC -> MAR -> Address Bus -> Memory -> Data Bus -> MDR -> IR; PC) Tj
T*
(incremented\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
