/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.5 System Bus Interconnections and Bandwidth Theory) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Data Bus: Bidirectional bus carrying raw data values between CPU, memory, and) Tj
T*
(peripherals. Width determines word size \(32-bit, 64-bit\).) Tj
T*
(* Address Bus: Unidirectional bus driven by CPU carrying physical memory addresses.) Tj
T*
(Width N determines maximum addressable memory capacity = 2^N bytes.) Tj
T*
(* Control Bus: Carrying synchronization signals \(Memory Read, Memory Write, I/O Read,) Tj
T*
(I/O Write, Bus Request, Bus Grant, Interrupt Request, Clock\).) Tj
T*
(* Bus Bandwidth Formula: Bandwidth \(Bytes/sec\) = Bus Width \(Bytes\) x Bus Frequency) Tj
T*
(\(Hz\) x Transfers per Clock.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([PROBLEM 1: Register-Level Trace of Instruction Fetch-Execute Cycle]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Trace the step-by-step register states during the execution of an) Tj
T*
(assembly instruction "ADD [0x0500]" \(Opcode: Add content of memory location 0x0500 to) Tj
T*
(Accumulator\). Initial conditions: PC = 0x0200, Accumulator \(ACC\) = 0x002A \(Decimal 42\).) Tj
T*
(Memory location 0x0200 holds instruction opcode 0xA10500. Memory location 0x0500 holds) Tj
T*
(data 0x0015 \(Decimal 21\).) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Register Transfer Language \(RTL\) Trace:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Fetch Cycle Step 1: MAR <- PC \(MAR loaded with address 0x0200\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Fetch Cycle Step 2: Control Unit emits Memory Read. MDR <- Memory[MAR] \(MDR) Tj
T*
(receives 0xA10500\). PC <- PC + 1 \(PC becomes 0x0201\).) Tj
T*
(* 3. Fetch Cycle Step 3: IR <- MDR \(Instruction Register loaded with 0xA10500\).) Tj
T*
(* 4. Decode Cycle: Control Unit decodes IR: Opcode = ADD, Operand Address = 0x0500.) Tj
T*
(* 5. Execute Cycle Step 1 \(Operand Fetch\): MAR <- 0x0500; Control Unit emits Memory) Tj
T*
(Read; MDR <- Memory[0x0500] \(MDR receives 0x0015\).) Tj
T*
(* 6. Execute Cycle Step 2 \(ALU Operation\): ALU adds ACC \(0x002A\) + MDR \(0x0015\) =) Tj
T*
(0x003F \(Decimal 63\).) Tj
T*
(* 7. Writeback Cycle: ACC <- 0x003F. Status flags \(Zero, Sign, Overflow\) updated.) Tj
T*
(Cycle completes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
